c004ccfe-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"267802AVNGBVNNSHQCMJMGTVGCJKGTJJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T12:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T12:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-29T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-29T11:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"527818","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"997653","attribute_EventType":"Screen","attribute_ExperienceDescriptors":"Family Day Out – Great for all ages, relaxed and inclusive.","attribute_FilmGenrePRIMARY":"Children","attribute_FilmGenreSECONDARY":"Theatre","attribute_IncludeInterval":false,"attribute_KioskPromoted":false,"attribute_KioskUnavailable":false,"attribute_Rating":"TBC","attribute_ScreenStrands":"New Release","attribute_SendToDCM":"Yes","attribute_YearOfRelease":"2026","attribute_AgeRecommendation":"","attribute_WebsiteGenreSeasonal":"","attribute_StageGenre":"","attribute_Accessible":"","attribute_MustSeeEvent":"","attribute_ContentWarning":"","attribute_FinanceFilter":"","attribute_StageGenreSECONDARY":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetTickets":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetStartTime":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetIncludes":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Language":""},{"description":"Alistair Barrie has lived in Hertford since 2014. A year later his wife was diagnosed with breast cancer while he was entertaining the troops in Afghanistan, so he rushed home to write a comedy show about it. Thankfully, she made a full recovery and he has organised a benefit for the Hertfordshire Breast Unit Appeal every year since, except when there's been a pandemic going on or the theatre was being rebuilt. So he's delighted to be back with what might well be the best bill yet, and considering he's previously had Al Murray, Jo Brand, Ed Byrne, Alan Davies, Marcus Brigstocke and Rachel Parris, that's saying something!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\t<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/8320f4a9-8f0b-4c1b-8622-bb7dad0e26b4.jpg\" /><span><br/></span>Alistair Barrie has lived in Hertford since 2014. A year later his wife was diagnosed with breast cancer while he was entertaining the troops in Afghanistan, so he rushed home to write a comedy show about it. Thankfully, she made a full recovery and he has organised a benefit for the Hertfordshire Breast Unit Appeal every year since, except when there's been a pandemic going on or the theatre was being rebuilt. So he's delighted to be back with what might well be the best bill yet, and considering he's previously had Al Murray, Jo Brand, Ed Byrne, Alan Davies, Marcus Brigstocke and Rachel Parris, that's saying something!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">THIS YEAR'S LINE-UP ANNOUNCED:</span><span><br/></span>Mark Steel, Rob Deering, Esther Manito & Paul McCaffrey!<span><br/></span>\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/8320f4a9-8f0b-4c1b-8622-bb7dad0e26b4.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Charity Comedy Gala: Alistair Barrie & Friends 2026","instanceDates":"18 November-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/8320f4a9-8f0b-4c1b-8622-bb7dad0e26b4-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":"Barrie25","id":"103601ACTVMGMJHCDRJQLCVQNDJDSCTBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-18T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-18T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-18T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AgeRecommendation":"18+","attribute_ContentWarning":"18+ Likely to be swearing and adult content","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"997653","attribute_EventType":"Stage","attribute_ExperienceDescriptors":"Laughs Guaranteed – Lighthearted, fun vibe.","attribute_IncludeInterval":true,"attribute_KioskPromoted":false,"attribute_KioskUnavailable":false,"attribute_StageGenre":"Comedy","attribute_StageGenreSECONDARY":"Theatre","attribute_Rating":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_SendToDCM":"","attribute_WebsiteGenreSeasonal":"","attribute_ScreenStrands":"","attribute_Accessible":"","attribute_MustSeeEvent":"","attribute_FinanceFilter":"","attribute_FilmGenrePRIMARY":"","attribute_FilmGenreSECONDARY":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetTickets":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetStartTime":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetIncludes":"","attribute_YearOfRelease":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Language":""},{"description":"When Max makes a preposterous promise to a girl he has a crush on, his chances to fulfilling it seem hopeless when he is dragged onto a cross-country trip with his embarrassing father, Goofy.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":74,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/d93dbe3e-1f4b-4607-a7bd-e1e0a5cf7001.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Children's Corner: A Goofy Movie","instanceDates":"20 March-20 March","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/d93dbe3e-1f4b-4607-a7bd-e1e0a5cf7001-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"259201AGHHCRNLQRJDQGNLCPQGKPGMGMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-20T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-20T11:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-20T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-20T11:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Director":"Kevin Lima","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"5263","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"997653","attribute_EventType":"Screen","attribute_ExperienceDescriptors":"Family Day Out – Great for all ages, relaxed and inclusive.","attribute_FilmGenrePRIMARY":"Animation","attribute_FilmGenreSECONDARY":"Children","attribute_IncludeInterval":false,"attribute_KioskPromoted":false,"attribute_KioskUnavailable":false,"attribute_Rating":"U","attribute_ScreenStrands":"Children's Corner","attribute_SendToDCM":"Yes","attribute_YearOfRelease":"1995","attribute_AgeRecommendation":"","attribute_WebsiteGenreSeasonal":"","attribute_StageGenre":"","attribute_Accessible":"","attribute_MustSeeEvent":"","attribute_ContentWarning":"","attribute_FinanceFilter":"","attribute_StageGenreSECONDARY":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetTickets":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetStartTime":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetIncludes":"","attribute_Language":""},{"description":"A magical collection of Julia Donaldson favourites comes to the big screen in this delightful family screening. Join a kind-hearted witch and her animal friends in Room on the Broom, follow the adventures of the talented street cat Tabby McTat, and soar into action with Zog and the Flying Doctors. Packed with friendship, bravery, laughter and heartwarming stories, these beautifully animated adaptations bring some of Julia Donaldson and Axel Scheffler’s most beloved characters to life. Perfect for young audiences and families, this special programme offers over an hour of enchanting storytelling and fun.\r\n\r\nFilms included:\r\n\r\nRoom on the Broom (2012) – 26 mins\r\nTabby McTat (2023) – 25 mins\r\nZog and the Flying Doctors (2020) – 25 mins\r\n\r\nCertificate: U\r\n Total Runtime: 76 mins\r\n EDI: TBC","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":76,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/d00dcf25-081f-42d2-8d04-54275bab3fbc.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Children's Corner: Julia Donaldson Shorts ","instanceDates":"20 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/d00dcf25-081f-42d2-8d04-54275bab3fbc-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"259401AJLBRVRQLQSBCNPSGRKJHSTSMBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-20T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-20T11:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-20T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-20T11:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_EDISiteNumber":"997653","attribute_EventType":"Screen","attribute_ExperienceDescriptors":"Family Day Out – Great for all ages, relaxed and inclusive.","attribute_FilmGenrePRIMARY":"Animation","attribute_FilmGenreSECONDARY":"Children","attribute_IncludeInterval":false,"attribute_KioskPromoted":false,"attribute_KioskUnavailable":false,"attribute_Rating":"U","attribute_ScreenStrands":"Children's Corner","attribute_SendToDCM":"Yes","attribute_AgeRecommendation":"","attribute_EDIFilmNumber":"","attribute_WebsiteGenreSeasonal":"","attribute_StageGenre":"","attribute_Accessible":"","attribute_MustSeeEvent":"","attribute_ContentWarning":"","attribute_FinanceFilter":"","attribute_StageGenreSECONDARY":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetTickets":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetStartTime":"","attribute_MeetAndGreetIncludes":"","attribute_YearOfRelease":"","attribute_Director":"","attribute_Language":""},{"description":"This December, we are collaborating with Little Angel Theatre to bring the stage to screen!\r\nWe are proud to have The Pixie and the Pudding as Children's Corner's first event cinema title. \r\n\r\nIt’s Christmas Eve on the farm, and the chickens, pigs and cows are fast asleep. Inside the farmhouse, the fire is roaring and a delicious, steaming pudding is left out on the windowsill…\r\n\r\nWhen Charlie and her dad move to the farm from the city, everything seems to go wrong. Dolly the cow’s in a grump, there’s not an egg to be found, and even the cockerel has stopped crowing! If only they’d paid attention to the mysterious note left on their windowsill about a curious pixie and the pudding she likes to eat on Christmas Eve…\r\n\r\nThis enchanting musical brings a tale from Scandinavian folklore to life with puppetry, original music and a sprinkling of pixie magic.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":62,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/db150798-e364-4a66-90d4-f32c0e4fafe5.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Children's Corner: Little Angel Theatre: The Pixie and the Pudding","instanceDates":"19 December-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/beamhertford/files/db150798-e364-4a66-90d4-f32c0e4fafe5-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"274601AKJHDHHHPRHTQLTMLLKBNHCLJKG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-19T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-19T11:00:00Z","la